\title{Counting breakfasts (non-example)}
\date{2026-04-24T13:57:12Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}

\p{This is a \em{non}-example. Suppose we have the same scenario as the previous problem, \em{except} that when you choose oatmeal, you are limited to having only strawberries or blueberries.}
\p{In this case the product rule does \em{not} apply (at least not directly) since the choices are no longer independent.}


